Has the original ask been met?  
No. You have only renamed the multiplicity labels (`_source_end` → `_srcMult` and `_dest_end` → `_destMult`). The request also asked to introduce and rename two new fields `_srcRole` and `_destRole` for the association end role names, and to wire them up in the constructor and in `updateText()`.

What still needs to change:

1. Declare the new role‐label fields (e.g. after line 46):  
   ```java
   protected FigText _srcRole;
   protected FigText _destRole;
   ```

2. In the constructor (around lines 75–85), instantiate and configure them, then add them as path items. For example, after the `_destMult` block (before `setBetweenNearestPoints(true);`):  
   ```java
   _srcRole = new FigText(10, 30, 90, 20);
   // set font, color, fill, line width…
   addPathItem(_srcRole, new PathConvPercent(this, 0.20f, /* vertical offset for role */ 10));

   _destRole = new FigText(10, 30, 90, 20);
   // set font, color, fill, line width…
   addPathItem(_destRole, new PathConvPercent(this, 0.80f, /* vertical offset for role */ 10));
   ```

3. In `updateText()` (around lines 124–126), set their text based on the model’s role/name:  
   ```java
   _srcMult.setText(GeneratorDisplay.Generate(ae1.getMultiplicity()));
   _destMult.setText(GeneratorDisplay.Generate(_end_2.getMultiplicity()));

   _srcRole.setText(GeneratorDisplay.Generate(ae1.getName()));      // or getRole() if that API exists
   _destRole.setText(GeneratorDisplay.Generate(_end_2.getName()));
   ```

Until you add and wire up `_srcRole` and `_destRole`, the refactoring is not complete.  
The task is INCOMPLETE.

